  "text": "��이터를 공격할 수 없는 무지개색\nLet \\( N \\) be the number of ordered triples \\((a, b, c)\\) of positive integers such that \\( a, b, c \\leq 3^6 = 729 \\) and \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\) is a multiple of \\( 3^7 = 2187 \\). We need to find the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 1000.\n\nFirst, we need to determine the conditions under which \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\) is a multiple of 2187. Since 2187 is \\( 3^7 \\), \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\) must be a multiple of 2187. This means that \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2187} \\).\n\nWe will use the fact that \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2187} \\) if and only if \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{729} \\) and \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\). This is because 2187 is \\( 729 \\times 3 \\).\n\n### Step 1: Counting the triples modulo 729\nWe need to count the number of triples \\((a, b, c)\\) such that \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{729} \\). This is equivalent to counting the number of solutions to \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{729} \\).\n\nSince \\( a, b, c \\leq 729 \\), we can use the fact that the cubes modulo 729 are uniformly distributed. Specifically, for each \\( a \\), there are exactly 27 values of \\( b \\) and \\( c \\) such that \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{729} \\). This is because the sum of cubes modulo 729 is a linear function, and the function is uniformly distributed.\n\nTherefore, the number of solutions modulo 729 is \\( 729^3 \\times 27 \\times 27 \\times 27 = 729^3 \\times 27^3 = 729^3 \\times 19683 = 729^3 \\times 2187 = 2187^3 \\).\n\n### Step 2: Counting the triples modulo 3\nWe need to count the number of triples \\((a, b, c)\\) such that \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\). This is equivalent to counting the number of solutions to \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\).\n\nThe cubes modulo 3 are:\n- \\( 0^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\)\n- \\( 1^3 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\)\n- \\( 2^3 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3} \\)\n\nSo, \\( a^3 + b^3 + c^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\) if and only if the sum of the cubes is 0 modulo 3. This can happen in the following ways:\n- \\( 0 + 0 + 0 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\)\n- \\( 1 + 1 + 1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\)\n- \\( 2 + 2 + 2 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\)\n\nEach of these cases occurs with probability 1/3 for each of \\( a, b, c \\). Therefore, the number of solutions modulo 3 is \\( 3^3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 = 3^3 \\times 3^3 = 3^6 = 729 \\).\n\n### Step 3: Combining the results\nThe total number of solutions is the product of the number of solutions modulo 729 and modulo 3. Therefore, \\( N = 2187^3 \\times 729 \\).\n\nTo find the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 1000, we need to compute \\( 2187^3 \\times 729 \\mod 1000 \\). Since \\( 2187 \\equiv 187 \\pmod{1000} \\), we need to compute \\( 187^3 \\times 729 \\mod 1000 \\).\n\nFirst, compute \\( 187^3 \\mod 1000 \\):\n\\[ 187^2 = 34969 \\equiv 969 \\pmod{1000} \\]\n\\[ 187^3 = 187 \\times 969 = 180363 \\equiv 363 \\pmod{1000} \\]\n\nNext, compute \\( 363 \\times 729 \\mod 1000 \\):\n\\[ 363 \\times 729 = 266547 \\equiv 547 \\pmod{1000} \\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( N \\) is divided by 1000 is \\( \\boxed{547} \\).",
